;;; An hrule's premise `(says (or …))` loads and proposes nothing —
;;; M1f **W83**, register row `W83/pattern-argument-hrule`, filed by S1f.7.3 (T1f.7.3.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, the fact `(says (paid Ann))`, and an hrule that supposes a guest
;;; welcome where it is said they paid or are welcome, `(says (or (paid ?g) (welcome
;;; ?g)))`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `or` heads no fact: refused at load, at the pattern, one line, on every command.
;;; With `(says (paid ?g))` H is `(welcome Ann)` and R is two states.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads; the hrule's premise matches nothing, H is
;;; empty and R is {∅}, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.3 (T1f.7.3.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation says Claim :why "it is said that {?1}")
(relation welcome Guest :why "{?1} is welcome")
(says (paid Ann))
(hrule guess () :match (and (is-a ?g Guest) (says (or (paid ?g) (welcome ?g)))) :assert (welcome ?g) :why "suppose {?g} is welcome")
(query :goal (welcome ?g))
